  "venue": "mcdonalds",
  "note": "Provenance for the dish photographs shipped under site/img/mcdonalds/. Repo-only record (ADR 0047): no screen renders any of this, and nothing under site/ refers to it.",
  "retrieved": "2026-08-16",
  "rights": {
    "holder": "McDonald's Corporation / McDonald's Restaurants (New Zealand) Ltd",
    "licence": "none — all rights reserved",
    "basis": "The venue's own product photography, taken from the public New Zealand menu pages at mcdonalds.co.nz / mcdonalds.com/nz, and used to depict that venue's own named products on its own menu listing. Not openly licensed. The owner authorised this route on 2026-08-16: 'If you can get open licensed photos that look great then lets do that, otherwise go ahead with the mcdonalds photos.'",
    "attributionRequired": false,
    "ifChallenged": "Remove the files under site/img/mcdonalds/ and the image/alt fields from site/data/restaurants/mcdonalds.json. The dish rows render without a photo."
  },
  "whyNotOpenlyLicensed": "Wikimedia Commons was searched per dish. Public-domain studio photographs do exist for some items (Evan-Amos: Big Mac, McChicken, Filet-O-Fish, Egg and Sausage & Egg McMuffin, Quarter Pounder, apple pie; Chris Woodrich: fries, 10-piece nuggets). They were rejected on three specific grounds rather than on principle: (1) they are opaque photographs on their own white background, whereas every shipped image is a transparent cutout that takes the card's colour in light and dark mode — one opaque tile among them reads as a fault; (2) several depict a different country's product or packaging (the PD fries carton carries the Canadian maple-leaf arches; the PD apple pie is the US baked pie shown split open, not the NZ sleeve); (3) the remaining candidates for NZ-only items are all CC BY or CC BY-SA, requiring visible attribution, and none is a product shot — the only NZ Big Arch photo on Commons is a whole meal tray, the only McCafé flat white is a Hong Kong cup beside a ciabatta. No NZ-only item (Big Brekkie Burger, Massive McMuffin, Thickshake, Frozen Coke, Hot Fudge Sundae) has any usable Commons image at all.",
  "processing": "Fetched once at authoring time as 800px transparent PNG (Scene7 fmt=png-alpha), then trimmed to the product's alpha bounding box and re-centred on a 720x540 frame at 86% fill, so all 41 are framed identically; encoded as WebP q0.82 via a canvas, which also drops every metadata segment (no EXIF, no GPS). 720x540 is 2x the 358x268.5 CSS box measured in a real browser at 390px, and matches the 4/3 aspect-ratio .dish-photo already declares. There is no build step: these files are the shipped artefact.",
